  "result": "Perfect! All 126 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added tier-based automatic discounts:**\n\n**Updated `src/customers.js`:**\n- Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` object with discount percentages for each tier:\n  - `gold: 5%`\n  - `silver: 2.5%`\n  - `standard: 0%`\n- One place to configure all tier discounts (centralized)\n\n**Updated `createInvoice` function:**\n- Now looks up customer to get their tier\n- For each line without explicit `discountPercent`, applies the customer's tier discount\n- If a line has explicit `discountPercent` (even if `0`), that **always wins** over tier discount\n- Only stores `discountPercent` on lines when it's non-zero (keeps lines clean)\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- Line with no `discountPercent` \u2192 gets customer's tier discount automatically\n- Line with explicit `discountPercent` (even `0`) \u2192 uses that, ignores tier discount\n- This allows overriding tier discounts on a per-line basis\n\n**Added 7 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Gold tier automatic discount (5%)\n- Silver tier automatic discount (2.5%)\n- Standard tier no discount (no field set)\n- Explicit discount overrides tier discount\n- Zero discount explicitly overrides tier\n- Multiple lines with tier discount applied\n- Mix of tier-discounted and explicitly-discounted lines\n\n**Updated existing tests:**\n- Adjusted render tests to use standard tier customers or explicitly set discount to 0\n- Updated invoiceTotals test to verify discounts are applied\n\nAll 126 tests pass \u2705",
